title: Patron Contributions
subtitle: Raise political capital from the Caucus's patrons.
is-card: true
tags: caucus_affairs
card-image: img/card_credits.svg
view-if: contributions_timer <= 0
on-arrival: turn_actions += 1; contributions_timer = 6; last_card_timer = "contributions"
new-page: true

= Patron Contributions

Politics in the Galactic Senate runs on favours and credits. The Caucus has friends who can provide both, at a price.

- @core: Appeal to wealthy Core patrons.
- @grassroots: Appeal to the member worlds directly.
- @guilds: Accept a generous offer from guild-linked donors.
- @easy_discard

@core
subtitle: +2 political capital. The Rimward wing dislikes it.
on-arrival: capital += 2; rimward_dissent += 7; pacifist_dissent += 2

Alderaanian nobles and Chandrilan bankers write generous cheques. The Rimward wing grumbles about "the Caucus of the comfortable".

@grassroots
subtitle: +1 political capital, a little more faith in the Republic and broader support.
on-arrival: capital += 1; faith += 0.5; core_rc += 0.5; colonies_rc += 0.5; midrim_rc += 0.5; outer_rc += 0.5

Small donations pour in from a hundred worlds. It is not much money, but it is a great deal of goodwill.

@guilds
view-if: difficulty < 1
subtitle: +3 political capital. The guilds will expect something; the Caucus will not like it.
on-arrival: capital += 3; guild_relation += 4; corruption += 1.5; rimward_dissent += 12; pacifist_dissent += 4; inst_dissent += 3; guild_money += 1

The money arrives through three intermediaries and a charitable foundation on Muunilinst. Nobody asks too many questions. That is rather the point.
